---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - Kery"
  description="Privacy policy for kery.dev and Kery Cloud."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-inner">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: April 4, 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        “Kery” refers to Kery Cloud and this website (<strong>kery.dev</strong>). This policy describes how we handle
        information when you visit the site or use the service.
      </p>

      <h2>2. This website (kery.dev)</h2>
      <p>
        The static marketing site is designed not to require accounts. We do not intentionally collect personal
        data through forms on this site. Our hosting provider may process standard server or edge logs (such as IP
        address, user agent, and request path) for security and reliability - refer to your host’s documentation
        for retention and subprocessors.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use analytics tools such as Google Analytics, Vercel Web Analytics, and PostHog to understand site
        traffic, page performance, referral sources, and product interest. These tools may process technical
        information such as IP address, browser, device, referrer, pages viewed, and interaction events.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Kery Cloud</h2>
      <p>
        When you use Kery Cloud, information you provide to operate the service may be processed, including account
        details, connected project configuration, test credentials, prompts, screenshots, run history, and reports.
        We use this information to provide and secure the service and make results available to your workspace.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Kery may rely on third-party providers to host the website and service, process payments, or provide
        integrations. AI provider requests may include prompts and the context needed to run a check. Those providers
        process information under their own terms and privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information for as long as needed to provide the service, meet legal obligations, resolve disputes,
        and enforce our agreements. We use safeguards designed to protect information, though no online service can
        guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict certain personal
        data. To make a privacy request, use the contact channels published on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the product and site evolve. Material changes will be reflected by updating the
        date above and, where appropriate, an announcement on this site or in the product.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent through the contact channels published on this site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: 6rem;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    min-height: 60vh;
  }

  .legal-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-inner h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal-inner h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-inner p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-inner a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .legal-inner a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
</style>
